.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-33-
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-34-### 1.1 Normative baseline
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-35-
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-36-The current protocol already establishes the correct security boundary:
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-37-
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md:38:- Skill packages and manifests are untrusted, and an installer **must not execute package-provided code while resolving, validating, auditing, or installing** ([core protocol, lines 63–69](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/57c1f56846d221ecc55786bd3c2467ec32f11730/protocol/core.md#L63-L69)).
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-39-- Manifests are strict JSON validated by schema and semantic rules; unknown fields fail ([core protocol, lines 9–20](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/57c1f56846d221ecc55786bd3c2467ec32f11730/protocol/core.md#L9-L20)).
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-40-- Schema versions 1–5 expose only `script` and `system` commands ([core protocol, lines 123–165](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/57c1f56846d221ecc55786bd3c2467ec32f11730/protocol/core.md#L123-L165); [common schema](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/57c1f56846d221ecc55786bd3c2467ec32f11730/schemas/v1/common.schema.json#L49-L72)). A script is copied; a system command is resolved. There is no compilation model.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-41-- Dependency closure uses deterministic provider-first topological order ([core protocol, lines 262–280](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/57c1f56846d221ecc55786bd3c2467ec32f11730/protocol/core.md#L262-L280)).
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-42-- The profile requires all non-mutating checks before materialization, a side-effect-free dry-run, rollback on materialization failure, and consumer/GC work last ([manager profile, lines 50–80](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/57c1f56846d221ecc55786bd3c2467ec32f11730/profiles/manager.md#L50-L80)).
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-43-- A runtime cache is currently keyed by skill and commit. Existing entries may be reused only after required paths are verified ([manager profile, lines 91–112](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/57c1f56846d221ecc55786bd3c2467ec32f11730/profiles/manager.md#L91-L112)).
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-44-- The install marker contains source/context identity but no build identity or artifact receipt ([install-marker-v1 schema](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/57c1f56846d221ecc55786bd3c2467ec32f11730/schemas/v1/install-marker-v1.schema.json)).
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md:45:- Capability declarations and successful audits are visibility and policy gates, not a sandbox and not proof that package code is safe to execute ([security model, lines 13–38](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/57c1f56846d221ecc55786bd3c2467ec32f11730/SECURITY.md#L13-L38)).
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-46-
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md:47:The build-driver design therefore must preserve a stronger rule than “the manifest declared execution”: installation cannot hand control to package-selected programs at all.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-48-
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-49-### 1.2 Go manager (`curator`) at `origin/main`
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-50-
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-51-The Go manager supports schemas 1–5 and only script/system commands ([skill types](https://github.com/relux-works/curator/blob/17804ceae42d3bb62abf6e8a9d9cbef6dd5370b8/internal/skillspec/types.go)). Runtime installation copies declared roots or one script and writes a shim; it has no compiler path ([installer, lines 353–420](https://github.com/relux-works/curator/blob/17804ceae42d3bb62abf6e8a9d9cbef6dd5370b8/internal/install/install.go#L353-L420)). The marker model has no build receipt ([marker model, lines 47–70](https://github.com/relux-works/curator/blob/17804ceae42d3bb62abf6e8a9d9cbef6dd5370b8/internal/marker/marker.go#L47-L70)).
--
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-79-
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-80-Treat all of the following as attacker-controlled input:
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-81-
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-82-- the repository snapshot, including source, `go.mod`, `go.sum`, `vendor/`, filenames, build constraints, compiler directives, embedded files, assembly, host objects, and file sizes;
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md:83:- both manifest spellings and all manifest fields;
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-84-- refs, registry data, cached source/runtime entries, and stale install markers until validated;
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-85-- build-receipt and artifact bytes as untrusted parser/hash inputs; their eligibility for reuse additionally depends on the manager-protected-state boundary below;
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-86-- any executable artifact produced from the package;
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-87-- output text emitted while the compiler parses the package.
--
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-93-- manager-owned policy constants, staging directories, cache locks, transaction journal, and manager-created private build-cache root;
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-94-- operating-system ownership, permission/ACL, and link-safety enforcement for that private root;
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-95-- the cryptographic hash and canonical JSON implementations.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-96-
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md:97:The package must not influence toolchain selection through its snapshot, manifest, current directory, `PATH`, Go environment files, workspace files, or module `toolchain` directive.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-98-
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-99-The v1 cache trust model is deliberately local and explicit: an adversary may supply arbitrary package/cache candidate bytes but cannot write manager-protected state as the manager's operating-system principal or as a trusted administrator. Arbitrary same-principal code execution, administrator/root compromise, kernel compromise, and hostile storage below the operating system are outside this install-time invariant; any of them could replace every local marker and manager binary as well as a receipt. This is an honest boundary for the two current user-space managers. A deployment that cannot enforce or accept it MUST disable persistent cache reuse and rebuild from the revalidated snapshot; authenticated cross-principal provenance is a possible future protocol feature, not something a plain SHA-256 receipt supplies.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-100-
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-101-### 2.2 Security invariant
--
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-108-- **MUST NOT** launch the newly built artifact, including for version discovery, smoke testing, post-processing, or receipt generation;
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-109-- **MAY** pass untrusted source bytes to the fixed, trusted `go-v1` compiler pipeline described below;
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-110-- **MAY** perform fixed data transformations, hashing, copying, permission changes, and schema validation in manager code.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-111-
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md:112:“Compile-only” means the manager owns every executable and argument in the build process. It does not claim that a compiler is immune to malicious inputs. Compiler vulnerabilities and resource-exhaustion inputs remain threats, so the child process must receive filesystem, network, time, output-size, process-count, memory, and disk controls where the host supports them. The resulting binary remains untrusted package code and is executed only later, when a user explicitly invokes the installed command.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-113-
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-114-### 2.3 Explicitly forbidden operations
