.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-180-`csk-skill-v6.schema.json` is an exact legacy-name mirror with its own `$id` and title, as today.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-181-
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-182-`build_roots` is new in schema 6 and is the conservative, compiler-independent context boundary. Each entry names a raw-source directory used only for manager-owned compilation. It is excluded from agent-facing context before locale rendering, never copied into the commit-keyed runtime store, and never installed as generated output. Schema versions 1–5 continue to reject this unknown field. V1 intentionally does not allow `.` as either a build root or `source_dir`; a root-module package must move its Go module below a dedicated directory such as `build/`.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-183-
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md:184:### 3.2 Valid manifest example
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-185-
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-186-This example deliberately mixes a compiled command with an existing script command; command collision and activation rules apply uniformly to both.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-187-
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md-188-```json
